<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Onfim</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">13th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Onfim was a boy who lived in Novgorod in the thirteenth century, probably aged six or seven, known from a group of birchbark documents found by archaeologists in 1956. They contain his writing exercises, copied prayers and drawings of himself as a warrior on horseback slaying enemies. They are a rare record of childhood and schooling in medieval <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a>.</p></div>
